  "summary": "Alexandrina Victoria was born on 24 May 1819 at Kensington Palace and became Queen of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland on 20 June 1837, at the age of eighteen. She reigned until her death at Osborne House on 22 January 1901; her reign of 63 years and 216 days defined the Victorian era.",
